// The apex, laterite.dev — a placeholder, served as static assets by a Worker
// with no code. Third of three: `laterite-app` (app.), `laterite-docs` (docs.),
// this one (bare).
//
// It exists now because the apex was ANSWERING NOTHING while being advertised:
// the GitHub Pages redirect shim names laterite.dev in its canonical tag and
// its noscript fallback, so every crawler and every JS-less visitor following
// that shim was sent to a hostname with no record. A redirect rule would have
// closed that too, but a Worker is the thing the real landing page will be —
// so this is the same object, thinner, rather than scaffolding to tear down.
//
// `assets.directory` is ./public, NOT ./ — a bare directory would upload this
// config file alongside the page.
//
// No `not_found_handling`: the default is an honest 404. The app's
// single-page-application setting would answer every mistyped path with the
// landing page, which is wrong for a site that is one real file.
{
  "$schema": "../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "laterite-site",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-14",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./public",
  },
  "routes": [{ "pattern": "laterite.dev", "custom_domain": true }],
}
